### Example requests for the matchmaking API.
### Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client) or in IntelliJ,
### then click "Send Request" above a request. Run them top to bottom: later requests
### reuse ids from earlier responses via named requests (# @name).
###
### Start the stack first:  docker compose up --build   (or run the app against
### `docker compose up postgres redis kafka`)

@base = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Health

GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Players

# @name createPlayer
POST {{base}}/players
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "yagiz-{{$randomInt 1000 9999}}",
  "country": "TR"
}

###

@playerId = {{createPlayer.response.body.$.id}}

### Get the player
GET {{base}}/players/{{playerId}}

### Level up (+1 level, +25 coins). Entering a tournament needs level 20,
### so send this 19 times for a new player, or lower matchmaking.min-level.
POST {{base}}/players/{{playerId}}/level-up

### Create a player without a country: one is assigned at random
POST {{base}}/players
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "random-{{$randomInt 1000 9999}}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tournaments

# @name createTournament
POST {{base}}/tournaments

###

@tournamentId = {{createTournament.response.body.$.id}}

### Get the tournament
GET {{base}}/tournaments/{{tournamentId}}

### Enter the tournament. Returns 202 Accepted; matchmaking continues in the background.
### Expect 422 if the player is below the minimum level or can't pay the entry fee,
### and 409 if they already entered.
POST {{base}}/tournaments/{{tournamentId}}/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": {{playerId}}
}

### Entry status: QUEUED -> MATCHED -> FINISHED
# @name entry
GET {{base}}/tournaments/{{tournamentId}}/entries/{{playerId}}

### Players waiting per country
GET {{base}}/tournaments/{{tournamentId}}/queue

### Overall leaderboard
GET {{base}}/tournaments/{{tournamentId}}/leaderboard?limit=10

### Leaderboard for one country
GET {{base}}/tournaments/{{tournamentId}}/leaderboard?country=TR&limit=10

### Stop accepting entries
POST {{base}}/tournaments/{{tournamentId}}/close

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Matches

### Match standings. Uses the matchId from the entry request above,
### which is only set once the player has been matched.
GET {{base}}/matches/{{entry.response.body.$.matchId}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Error examples

### 404: unknown player
GET {{base}}/players/999999

### 400: validation error (blank username)
POST {{base}}/players
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": ""
}
